      "retained_opening_prose_exact": "The first part of this research companion records the direct odd-prime and weighted dyadic construc-\ntions, including the low-rank carrier repairs. This continuation returns to the earlier monomial and\nClifford branches. Their conclusions are not interchangeable. A genuine arithmetic candidate may have\nthe right dimension and conductor while failing to contain a prescribed full simple character. A finite\ncarrier may have enough dimension while failing the required action or marking. A compatible formal\ninterface may still await its actual arithmetic input.\nThe purpose here is to make those distinctions mathematically usable. We extract the precise restricted\nimplications, explain the negative results, and retain the surviving routes. The presentation includes\nelementary proofs where the argument is short enough to expose completely. Deeper arithmetic state-\nments are identified as inherited ordinary arguments with named classical inputs. No theorem in this\ncontinuation is newly certified by Lean.",
      "retained_opening_bbox_y_interval": [
        90,
        251
      ],
